WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.580
Having your ordinary life unceremoniously&nbsp;
change forever without a moment’s notice is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.980
something that people can often find themselves&nbsp;
hoping for. Anything to break life’s monotony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.860
and change circumstances to make them more&nbsp;
interesting. Although, when that change comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:22.140
in the form of being trapped in an endless Ikea&nbsp;
outlet, it’s not exactly the different kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:27.420
circumstances that people usually hope for.
That was the situation that had befallen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.820
Winston not too long ago. What started as a&nbsp;
simplistic, straightforward shopping trip with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.740
the goal of purchasing some affordable, stylish&nbsp;
Swedish furniture had resulted in him having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.660
to adopt a completely different lifestyle.&nbsp;
You see, Winston was one of an untold number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:49.800
of people to have an encounter with SCP-3008,&nbsp;
better known colloquially as the Infinite Ikea.&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:55.740
Appearing as an ordinary store, those entering&nbsp;
through the doors of SCP-3008 find themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.920
in an unending labyrinth of aisles upon aisles&nbsp;
filled with flatpack homeware. It can be quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.240
the system shock, of course, especially&nbsp;
when people that find themselves inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:12.000
the Infinite Ikea learn that there’s no way to&nbsp;
escape, even by retracing their steps back the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.280
way they came. Doing so, they’ll only be met&nbsp;
with the disheartening realization that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.620
entrance isn’t where it was upon their arrival.
Now, at first, learning that you’ve lost your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:28.020
entire life and are doomed to spend the rest of&nbsp;
your days inside a limitless Ikea is admittedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:35.100
a lot to take in. Your friends, family, job, and&nbsp;
all your worldly possessions are now unreachable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.060
and everyone back home might likely&nbsp;
spend many years wondering what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.520
happened to you. But it’s not all bad news.
As previously mentioned, Winston wasn’t the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.440
only one to find himself in this predicament. Over&nbsp;
the years, countless people have found their way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.440
inside the Infinite Ikea. Given how expansive&nbsp;
the interior of the never-ending store was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.540
there has never been a way to know for certain&nbsp;
exactly how many people have come to reside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:06.480
within SCP-3008. But it's enough to populate&nbsp;
the number of small settlements that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.760
survivors have been able to establish inside.
By innovatively repurposing the materials around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:19.200
them, those that have found themselves to be&nbsp;
new denizens of SCP-3008. Imagine whole towns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.880
constructed from chairs and tables that have&nbsp;
been used as building materials to provide a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:29.400
place of sanctuary to those that need it when&nbsp;
they first arrive in the Infinite Ikea. Sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:35.280
it takes a pretty big adjustment to this new&nbsp;
lifestyle. But luckily, SCP-3008 provides for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.080
its inhabitants by automatically replenishing&nbsp;
the food within its canteen. Naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:45.360
it only offers items that are on the Ikea menu,&nbsp;
but that’s at least a consistent source of food&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:51.240
and nutrition for those dwelling in its aisles.
With food already taken care of, people inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:57.480
SCP-3008 didn’t even need to work. That was the&nbsp;
strangest part that Winston found himself having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:02.880
to adapt to when he first got to the settlement&nbsp;
of ‘Cookware’ named after the nearby sign that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:08.400
hung from the ceiling nearby, denoting one of&nbsp;
many departments of the store. It was odd to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.080
him how friendly everyone was, how much&nbsp;
the people trapped inside SCP-3008, cut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:18.060
off from the outside world forever seemed happy.
There were many who’d been there for the longest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:23.820
that even claimed it was a better way of life than&nbsp;
out there in the ‘real world’. Inside the Ikea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:29.100
there was a strong sense of community. Settlements&nbsp;
helped each other out with construction, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:34.860
because everyone was provided for, no-one had&nbsp;
any need for selfishness or greed. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:39.960
there was plenty of food to go around and&nbsp;
money had no relevance – ironic given that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:45.720
were all living inside a huge furniture store.
Witnessing all that helped Winston to adapt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:52.620
this new life inside SCP-3008, and made him feel&nbsp;
a lot better about being in this predicament. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:58.260
only real thing anyone inside the Infinite Ikea&nbsp;
had to worry about was the threat of the Staff.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:04.260
These were the tall, faceless humanoids with&nbsp;
elongated arms and legs that roamed the aisles of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:10.260
the furniture store while wearing distinctive Ikea&nbsp;
uniforms. Most of the time, they remained docile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:15.720
paying the human survivors little attention.
That is, until the fluorescent lights above&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.700
dimmed, signaling the beginning of night&nbsp;
time. The Staff usually became aggressive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:27.840
repeating the ominous phrase “The store is&nbsp;
now closed, please exit the building,” and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:33.420
attacking anyone they came into contact with.
Thanks to their ingenuity, the survivors in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:38.100
Ikea had constructed barriers around their&nbsp;
settlements to keep the Staff out. And that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:45.180
did the trick, repelling the faceless employees&nbsp;
come night. But little did anyone inside SCP-3008&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:50.880
realize that simple barricades wouldn’t stop an&nbsp;
entirely new threat from entering the store to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:57.720
disrupt their peaceful way of life. For outside&nbsp;
the Infinite Ikea, something wicked was stirring.&nbsp;

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.940
Meanwhile, at a facility belonging to the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation, a researcher by the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:09.480
of Corbin Donnel had recently been reassigned&nbsp;
to SCP-035. Also known as the Possessive Mask,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:15.540
this white porcelain mask could shift between a&nbsp;
comedy grin or a tragic frown. It also had the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:20.820
nasty trait of being an evil psychic artifact&nbsp;
that could manipulate anyone around it into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:27.480
placing the mask over their face. At that point,&nbsp;
SCP-035 would take full control of its wearer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:32.460
making them into a host for the mask&nbsp;
itself. So, would you like to take a guess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:38.220
as to what was happening to Researcher Donnel?
The voice in his head, that persuasive whisper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:45.480
it wouldn’t leave him alone. All day long, it&nbsp;
was there, but whenever Corbin was near SCP-035,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:49.980
it got even louder. And as the days he&nbsp;
was studying the Possessive Mask went on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:55.380
the whisper became a shout. The screams to&nbsp;
put on the mask were taunting him, keeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:01.020
him awake at night, tormenting him all through the&nbsp;
waking day. Until, eventually, he’d had enough.&nbsp;

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:07.140
Given that SCP-035 produced a corrosive, black&nbsp;
substance that usually melted anything around it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:12.300
the mask had to be periodically taken out of its&nbsp;
containment case so that the container housing it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:18.000
could be replaced. And it was during one of these&nbsp;
transfers that Researcher Donnel calmly swept in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.700
pushed away the guards taking it out of its melted&nbsp;
case before they could place it in a new one. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:29.280
aggression from the Researcher caught the security&nbsp;
personnel by surprise, as did what he did next.&nbsp;

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.200
Not caring what the Possessive Mask would do&nbsp;
to him, Corbin lifted the white porcelain to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.280
his face. He wasn’t even aware that the&nbsp;
containment breach alarms were sounding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:43.680
all that noise sank into the background as the&nbsp;
psychic voice in his head got louder than it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:49.380
had ever been before. There wasn’t even so much as&nbsp;
a split second awareness from Researcher Donnel of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:55.140
the searing pain as the dark sludge oozing from&nbsp;
the mask made contact with his skin, melting his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.140 --> 00:07:03.360
face as he wore SCP-035. By that point, it was&nbsp;
already too late. The Possessive Mask had full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:09.420
control. Corbin’s body wasn’t his own any more.&nbsp;
Although it still moved, walking quickly out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:14.520
the room and through the halls of the Foundation&nbsp;
facility, the researcher beneath was already dead.&nbsp;

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:20.220
There was only SCP-035, piloting&nbsp;
its newest host to freedom.&nbsp;

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:24.720
Of course, while a containment breach was&nbsp;
still an urgent matter, the Foundation knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:31.320
that SCP-035’s biggest weakness was itself. The&nbsp;
black secretion that poured out of the Possessive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:36.360
Mask would melt anything it came into contact&nbsp;
with, and would ultimately cause the body of its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:43.020
host to melt into nothing. Once this happened,&nbsp;
it would be far easier to re-contain SCP-035,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:47.760
someone would merely have to carefully pick it&nbsp;
up and place it back in the containment case.&nbsp;

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:54.720
However, SCP-035 knew this too. The mask&nbsp;
itself was cunning, it hadn’t just picked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.700
Researcher Donnel at random to be its new&nbsp;
vehicle, it wanted him specifically because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:07.140
of his previous posting. Before he had worked with&nbsp;
SCP-035, Corbin had been stationed to observe any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:14.220
potential changes at the entrance of… SCP-3008.
As it stayed firmly on the researcher’s face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:18.180
using him to carry itself out of the&nbsp;
Foundation site it had been trapped in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:24.780
SCP-035 was scouring the remnants of Corbin’s&nbsp;
mind. It used its innate psychic abilities to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:30.840
plunder the depths of his brain, looking for&nbsp;
information. The location of SCP-3008 was right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:37.680
there, stored away safely in Researcher Donnel’s&nbsp;
memories. As was the way to get there. And on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:44.820
top of that, the reason SCP-035 had taken such&nbsp;
an interest in making it to the Infinite Ikea.&nbsp;

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:49.500
During the Foundation’s many years&nbsp;
of study and exploration of SCP-3008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:54.600
they had come to learn that not all of the&nbsp;
survivors inside the Infinite Ikea had originated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:59.760
from the same universe. The current theory was&nbsp;
that entrances to the endless furniture store&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:05.520
existed simultaneously in multiple realities,&nbsp;
meaning that the people now living alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:12.780
each other inside SCP-3008 were actually from&nbsp;
varying different worlds across the multiverse.&nbsp;

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:17.340
Now, if you were incredibly cunning,&nbsp;
incredibly clever, and incredibly sick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:22.140
of being held captive by the Foundation, then&nbsp;
perhaps you could figure out a way to navigate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:27.240
your way through the Infinite Ikea. You could&nbsp;
enter through the front door in one universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:33.660
and then exit into another. And of course, that&nbsp;
was what the Possessive Mask was planning to do.&nbsp;

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:39.720
As it approached the main entrance of SCP-3008,&nbsp;
the black gunge leaking out of the mask had almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:44.460
destroyed what was left of Researcher Corbin&nbsp;
Donnel. It wiped more of the corrosive secretion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:50.160
onto the guards stationed at the Infinite&nbsp;
Ikea, melting through them as SCP-035 made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:56.160
its way inside. First things first, the mask knew&nbsp;
it had to find itself a new body to pilot, before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:02.100
Corbin’s expired… and it didn’t take long for&nbsp;
the Possessive Mask to happen across an unwitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:07.380
candidate between the aisles of flatpack tables.
At around the same time that this was happening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:13.920
Winston – having long since gotten used to the&nbsp;
rhythm of life inside SCP-3008 – was on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.480
way to the food court. He knew the route&nbsp;
by heart now, and as he strolled closer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:23.640
he was pondering over what he’d help himself to&nbsp;
today from the menu. But it was while making his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:28.800
way there that he noticed something; or rather,&nbsp;
he noticed not noticing something that he usually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:34.260
did. There were no Staff anywhere around.
Although they didn’t pay the survivors any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:39.480
mind during the day, when the lights of the Ikea&nbsp;
were on, Winston knew that the Staff members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:44.580
were always present. There were usually a couple&nbsp;
milling about the aisles he had to pass in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:50.100
to get from the settlement of Cookware to the food&nbsp;
hall. But today, there were none. And while this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:55.320
wouldn’t usually be any cause for alarm, it kept&nbsp;
playing on Winston’s mind as he sat down to eat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.320 --> 00:11:01.380
his plate of Swedish meatballs. He’d been inside&nbsp;
SCP-3008 for such a long time that he’d become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:06.000
accustomed to the routine of living there, and&nbsp;
the absence of the Staff immediately stuck out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:10.740
as something that was out of its usual place.
Finishing his food, Winston asked around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:16.260
talking with his fellow residents of the Infinite&nbsp;
Ikea, asking if any of them had encountered any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:20.700
of the tall, faceless Staff members on&nbsp;
their way to get their meals. Each and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:25.020
every one of them that he asked, from varying&nbsp;
different settlements, all answered the same,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:31.020
that they hadn’t spotted any Staff all day. As&nbsp;
much as they were a minor threat to the human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:37.320
beings living in the Infinite Ikea, the absence of&nbsp;
the store’s only other residents kept playing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:43.140
Winston’s mind. Whatever was going on, the Staff&nbsp;
seemingly vanishing couldn’t mean anything good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:48.660
and so he decided to venture out into the&nbsp;
aisles to figure out what exactly was going on.&nbsp;

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:55.560
What he found was unlike anything that&nbsp;
anyone had seen in SCP-3008 before.&nbsp;

00:11:55.560 --> 00:12:01.140
It took Winston several long and uneventful&nbsp;
hours to catch even a momentary glimpse of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:05.220
a Staff member, he almost felt like someone&nbsp;
trekking through a forest looking to get a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:11.040
sighting of Bigfoot, or some other elusive urban&nbsp;
legend. But as the third hour became the fourth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:16.680
he spotted a hint of movement between the aisles.&nbsp;
Following at a safe distance, listening out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:21.240
the slightest sounds, Winston couldn’t help&nbsp;
but think he detected the noise of something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:27.180
heavy being dragged along the store floor.
Peeking out from between the aisles, he saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:32.700
them. A huge group of Staff members were huddled&nbsp;
in a display dining room, only there was something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:38.040
different about them all. They all still retained&nbsp;
their recognizable tall and humanoid shapes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:42.720
with long disproportionally long limbs. But&nbsp;
there was something smeared over the Staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:47.520
a dark, oily black substance that seemed&nbsp;
to melt through the floor as it dripped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:53.100
off them. From his hiding place, Winston soon&nbsp;
saw where that substance had originated from.&nbsp;

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:58.500
The thing being dragged across the floor was&nbsp;
another Staff member, looking more normal than the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:03.600
rest. One of the others, covered in the corrosive&nbsp;
sludge, was gripping it by the collar of its Ikea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:08.820
polo shirt and bringing it through the group.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, the ‘ordinary’ creature was thrashing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:13.980
and flailing its lengthy arms around, trying to&nbsp;
get free. It was dragged up to a Staff member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:18.660
in the middle of the group, which turned around&nbsp;
and shocked Winston at the strange sight of it.&nbsp;

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:25.080
This Staff member, evidently the leader, had&nbsp;
a face. Or rather, it was wearing a mask.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:32.160
SCP-035 was now affixed firmly to the slender,&nbsp;
faceless being, its expression locked in a wide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:37.440
grin that seemed to convey a twisted sense&nbsp;
of glee. Its black secretion didn’t seem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:42.480
be affecting its new host in the same way it&nbsp;
usually did, the body of the Staff member it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:47.520
was now piloting didn’t seem to dissolve. As&nbsp;
the uncorrupted Staff creature was presented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:53.460
to the masked leader, SCP-035 compelled its&nbsp;
newfound followers to restrain their prisoner.&nbsp;

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:58.740
The workers within SCP-3008 didn’t have much&nbsp;
in the way of their own free will or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:04.140
personalities to speak of. They did, however, seem&nbsp;
to share some sort of connection to each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:09.540
a hive mind of sorts. So, presented with a&nbsp;
powerful psychic force like the Possessive Mask,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:15.960
the entity had been able to not only take over&nbsp;
one Staff member as its new host, but spread its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:21.960
influence to the others. And while Winston watched&nbsp;
horrified, it unknowingly demonstrated this.&nbsp;

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:27.300
The captive Staff member was grabbed and held&nbsp;
by the others, its long arms and legs pulled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:32.640
apart. The huddled group lifted it up off the&nbsp;
floor, so it couldn’t free itself and run off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:39.660
into the endless aisles of furniture. Wearing&nbsp;
SCP-035, the leader extended an arm, black ooze&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:44.220
dripping from it, the droplets burning holes&nbsp;
in the floor as it reached towards the faceless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:49.620
head of the restrained Staff member. It placed a&nbsp;
large hand over the faceless head of the captive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:55.740
more of the corrosive secretion passing onto&nbsp;
the new addition to SCP-035’s growing army.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.740 --> 00:15:00.720
As the black substance spread over the Staff&nbsp;
member, so did the influence of the Possessive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:05.760
Mask force its way into another vessel.
“I’m telling you; I know what I saw!”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:11.160
Winston protested after recounting the events&nbsp;
to the other settlers back at Cookware. “There’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:15.540
something else out there, something new and&nbsp;
dangerous, and it’s infecting the Staff!”&nbsp;

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:21.660
“It’s ridiculous,” replied Bryce, one of the&nbsp;
survivors who’d been there much longer. “I’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:25.260
been here for years, and I never even&nbsp;
heard of such a thing!” they yelled.&nbsp;

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.920
“I saw it with my own eyes,”&nbsp;
Winston argued. “It has a small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:33.120
army of them already under its control.”
“Even if what you’re saying is true,” someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:37.320
else chimed in. “What does it matter? We’ve&nbsp;
already got barriers that keep the Staff out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:41.340
and they only attack at night anyway.&nbsp;
Surely, even if this mask thing really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:46.200
is in control of them now, who cares?”
As if on cue, one of the lookouts at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:50.700
Cookware settlement started frantically trying&nbsp;
to get everyone’s attention. They pointed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:55.920
the ominous glow coming from just beyond the&nbsp;
nearby aisles filled with wardrobe frames. An&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.920 --> 00:16:00.180
orange flicker was visible, even under the&nbsp;
lights of the store, which were still on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:05.160
although blocked a little by thick plumes of&nbsp;
black smoke rising up towards the ceiling.&nbsp;

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:09.600
“That’s Lighting,” the lookout said in&nbsp;
shocked disbelief, stating the name of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:13.560
another nearby community of survivors that&nbsp;
was named after an Ikea store department.&nbsp;

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:17.880
“Something must’ve happened over there,”&nbsp;
Bryce declared. “Maybe it’s an electrical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.660
fire that’s gotten out of control.”
“It’s them,” Winston said solemnly.&nbsp;

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:27.060
“It can’t be them!” the older survivor snapped.&nbsp;
“The lights are still on, it’s still daytime in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:31.680
the store, and Staff never attack during the day.”
“I don’t think the rules are the same anymore!”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:36.540
Winston argued frustratedly. “There’s&nbsp;
no telling what that mask did to them.”&nbsp;

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:42.120
“Perhaps…” Bryce was trying desperately to come&nbsp;
up with a suggestion, but was clearly grasping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:46.860
at straws. “What if this mask can be reasoned&nbsp;
with? If it's more intelligent than the Staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.760
we can… we can negotiate! There&nbsp;
must be something it wants!”&nbsp;

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:55.140
“What do you think it wants? It wants this&nbsp;
place, this Ikea. And now it has control of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:59.940
enough Staff to form a small army. You think it’s&nbsp;
just gonna stop there? It’s coming for all of us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:04.560
and it won’t stop until it’s got this whole store&nbsp;
under its control! And if it has to wipe us out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:09.780
do that… well, it looks like it’s not hesitating.”
“So, what do we do?” a voice called meekly.&nbsp;

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:14.040
Winston turned to see the townsfolk of&nbsp;
Cookware had gathered, all looking up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:18.060
at him with terrified expressions on their&nbsp;
faces. He gazed back at each one of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:22.020
then looked back over at the smoke now&nbsp;
towering over where Lighting had been,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:28.020
and was now in flames. Who knew how many of the&nbsp;
settlers there were still alive? And how long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:34.800
would it be before SCP-035 and its new army did&nbsp;
the same to Cookware? Something had to be done.&nbsp;

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:38.940
“We need to get the word out!” Winston&nbsp;
announced to the other survivors. “I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:42.360
need our fastest to run over to the other&nbsp;
towns in the store. You each take one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:46.560
you pass on the message, and then you come back.&nbsp;
You know your way around well enough, so avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:50.760
anywhere you’d normally see Staff. Even if they&nbsp;
haven’t been corrupted, we can’t chance it.”&nbsp;

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:54.060
“What do we tell the other settlements?”&nbsp;
somebody in the crowd called.&nbsp;

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:58.260
“You tell them what’s going on. You say that&nbsp;
something has come here to threaten this Ikea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:02.580
and our way of life. This place isn’t where&nbsp;
any of us first came from, but it’s all of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:07.620
home now. It’s provided for us, but now it&nbsp;
needs us to defend it,” Winston explained.&nbsp;

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.400
“And how exactly are we going&nbsp;
to do that?” Bryce asked.&nbsp;

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:16.920
The lights had gone out, but although night&nbsp;
had fallen, it wasn’t dark yet. Standing with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:21.900
their fellow survivors from numerous other&nbsp;
settlements, the residents of SCP-3008 had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:27.060
fashioned flaming torches from the legs of&nbsp;
Ikea desks and tables. And that wasn’t all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:32.580
They were carrying makeshift weapons. Some had&nbsp;
spears crafted using curtain rails with sharp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:37.620
kitchen implements fashioned to the end. Others&nbsp;
had wardrobe doors in their hands to act as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:42.960
rudimentary shields. They were hardly warriors,&nbsp;
but as an army of corrupted Staff members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:49.140
lurched out of the darkness towards them, each&nbsp;
survivor of SCP-3008 knew what they had to do.&nbsp;

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:55.800
At the front of its army, towered the Staff member&nbsp;
with SCP-035 on its faceless head. The Possessive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.800 --> 00:19:01.980
Mask’s wide grin had shifted, now a long frown,&nbsp;
almost one of disgust at the amassed settlers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:07.380
who opposed it. As it raised an elongated arm&nbsp;
to command its horde, Winston raised a curtain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:11.640
rail spear into the air.
“FOR IKEA!” he yelled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:17.700
as the residents of SCP-3008 charged.
